; Meadow — NEW TerrainDefinition (habitat-tiers ruling, 2026-09-04 -> task-8-brief.md).
; VALUES BELOW ARE A PROPOSAL AWAITING HUMAN SIGN-OFF (same posture as every other
; terrain's cost/scale/model choices in this codebase; see barn.tres for the same
; convention on the buildings side).
;
; WHY IT EXISTS: rich grazing terrain, and the first real SOURCE for the long-dormant
; `flowers` habitat tag (AnimalDefinition.HABITAT_TAGS has carried `flowers` with no
; emitter since it was added — this closes that gap). Paired with Scrub as the second half
; of the new grazing-terrain split: Meadow is the `open_grass`-family pick (same emission
; as plain Grass, plus `flowers`), Scrub is the `browse`-family pick.
;
; emitted_tags = ["open_grass", "flowers"] is DECIDED by the habitat-tiers ruling
; (task-8-brief.md's table). No radius, no weight, no threshold — the v1 tag model
; (-> D-25) applies unchanged.
;
; cost = 0 — natural terrain, "nature is free" (terrain.md's one pricing rule, unchanged by
; this task).
;
; MODEL_SCENE: Meadow.tscn (CC0, Stylized Nature MegaKit) — see that scene's own header for
; full sourcing/scale detail. Single variant; a multi-variant look-pass is out of scope
; here, same posture Grass/Rock/Wild grass all started with before their own later passes.
;
; PLAYER-VISIBLE CONSEQUENCE: Meadow is a new, free-to-paint entry in the Terraform
; palette — flagged prominently per this task's brief, not buried in a count bump.
;
; No `fact_text` copy yet — Content Pipeline step 5 (Content Writer), explicitly out of
; scope for this task.
